                                                "sense_id": "204dfb36-5bc1-3b9a-9d37-6f8319e29201",
                                                "text": "He recalled that the big hill which served as their backdrop—the one that was always there despite the changing dunes—was known as Mazhatage, which was the Uygur word for “tomb.”"
